---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { contatti } from '../../data/sito.js';
---
<Base lang="en" title="Privacy and cookies · Desideri & Code" description="How I handle your data when you visit the site or request a quote." path="/en/privacy" alt="/privacy" scena={false}>
  <section class="pagina">
    <div class="wrap prosa">
      <span class="capitolo">Privacy and cookies</span>
      <h1>Your data, in plain words.</h1>
      <p><em>Draft to be completed with an accountant or privacy consultant before publication. The Italian version is the legally binding one.</em></p>
      <h2>Who handles the data</h2>
      <p>{contatti.nome} ({contatti.studio}){contatti.piva ? `, VAT no. ${contatti.piva}` : ''}, Milan, Italy. Email: <a href={`mailto:${contatti.email}`}>{contatti.email}</a>.</p>
      <h2>What I collect and why</h2>
      <p>When you fill in the quote form I collect your name, email, phone number, business and the choices you made for your project. I use them only to reply to you and prepare your quote (legal basis: pre-contractual steps you requested). I never sell or share them.</p>
      <p>Requests are saved in a Google spreadsheet and notified on Telegram (services of Google LLC and Telegram, which may process data outside the EU with the safeguards required by the GDPR). If you choose to send your project via WhatsApp or email, the message goes through your own account on those services.</p>
      <h2>How long</h2>
      <p>I keep request data for 24 months and then delete it, unless you become a client (in which case tax obligations apply).</p>
      <h2>Cookies and personalisation</h2>
      <p>The site only uses your browser's technical storage to remember your choices: your quote in progress, your cookie preference, the intro animation already seen and, if you personalise the site, your first name and your favourite colour. These stay on your device and are never sent to me. Analytics or advertising cookies (Google Analytics, Meta Pixel) only start if you press "OK" in the banner. You can change your mind at any time from the "Cookie preferences" link at the bottom of every page.</p>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask at any time to see, correct or delete your data, or object to its use, by writing to <a href={`mailto:${contatti.email}`}>{contatti.email}</a>. You can also lodge a complaint with the Italian Data Protection Authority (Garante per la protezione dei dati personali).</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
